  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Comprehensive and integrated life-saving Gender-Based Violence (GBV) response services to women, girls and young people affected by armed conflict in Mozambique&#x2019;s Mocimboa da Praia district with a special focus on returnees.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide critical protection interventions for conflict-affected returnees in Mocimboa da Praia district. This UNFPA project provides comprehensive GBV response services to vulnerable women and girls in order to prevent and respond to gender-based violence among conflict-affected communities. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 31,375 people, including 18,204 women, 9,767 children and 941 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
